WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
On Friday nights, many Jewish
families sing a poem from Proverbs:

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.420
a woman of valour.

3
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.500
The woman in the poem
runs a household, trades,

4
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.110
and buys a field.

5
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:16.760
Yet in Orthodox Jewish law, some women
are called agunot: chained women.

6
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:20.840
Their marriage is over in
practice, but they cannot remarry.

7
00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.350
How can a divorce be chained?

8
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.330
In this mission, you'll see how roles for
women and men differ across Jewish movements,

9
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.490
at home and in prayer.

10
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:36.450
Then you'll weigh up a hard question: can
women be fully equal to men in Judaism?

11
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.670
Your mission: find out how a
divorce can leave a woman chained.
